<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Sormovsky 43     arrived     barley	    2,821     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 212     13/10	 feed wheat	3,003     Europe</p>
<p>Federal Calumet  15/10	 barley	   21,091     U.S.</p>
<p>Black Sea	  15/10	 sunflower meal  3,900     Europe</p>
<p>Volzsky 37	 16/10	 barley	    2,195     Europe</p>
<p>Geroy Tripolia   16/10	 sunflower seed  1,060     Europe</p>
<p>				     wheat	     1,750</p>
<p>Sanem		16/10	 barley	    4,972     Europe</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	21/10	 corn	     25,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     wheat	    36,500</p>
<p>Szeregy Szare    22/10	 corn	     25,000     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	  18,000</p>
<p>				     soya	     14,000</p>
<p>Golden Sky	 30/10	 barley	   18,000     U.S.</p>
</text>
